      "justification": "The paper indeed computes the QWK ceiling from the same expert annotation process used to build the training data (Section 3.2.3/4.1) and does not report an independent expert panel or cross-domain generalization evaluation.",
      "status": "ok"
    },
    {
      "method": "baseline_cmp3_baseline_v2",
      "paper_id": "1AYy3T3Xjk",
      "weakness": "Disconnect between 'process-level' framing and model architecture: the evaluator receives the full raw dialogue and outputs dialogue-level scores without explicitly modeling temporal/causal structure or ITA internally; attribution is only evaluated as a separate task.",
      "reliable": 1,
      "error_type": "",
      "justification": "The paper states the model 'jointly produces two outputs' (scores, rationale) from dialogue D as a whole (Section 3.3.1) and never describes turn-level intermediate representations or ITA being fed as structured input to the scoring model.",
      "status": "ok"
    },
    {
      "method": "baseline_cmp3_baseline_v2",
      "paper_id": "1AYy3T3Xjk",
      "weakness": "Limited sample diversity: 81 undergraduates from two research-intensive universities, predominantly STEM, constraining generality of CREDO dimensions and results to arts/design/humanities.",
      "reliable": 1,
      "error_type": "",
      "justification": "The paper's own Limitations section confirms this: 'sample comprises 81 undergraduates from two research universities, with contexts primarily in STEM inquiry... does not cover the full landscape of arts/design.'",
      "status": "ok"
    },
    {
      "method": "baseline_cmp3_baseline_v2",
      "paper_id": "1AYy3T3Xjk",
      "weakness": "Unclear role of ITA in the evaluator pipeline: not clear whether ITA decomposition is provided as input to the fine-tuned model or used only during annotation.",
      "reliable": 1,
      "error_type": "",
      "justification": "Section 3.3.1 only says the model takes dialogue D and outputs scores/rationale; the paper never explicitly states whether ITA annotations are part of the model's input features, supporting the reviewer's ambiguity claim.",
      "status": "ok"
    },
    {
      "method": "baseline_cmp3_baseline_v2",
      "paper_id": "1AYy3T3Xjk",
      "weakness": "Missing details about training and ablation: ablation studies (w/o LoRA, w/o KD, Scores-only) and 17-sample refinement are referenced only to Appendix A which is not available, and λ_rat/λ_KD are unspecified.",
      "reliable": 1,
      "error_type": "",
      "justification": "The provided paper text explicitly states 'See Table A2 in Appendix A' and the appendix is noted as removed/not available, and no numeric values for λ_rat or λ_KD are given in the visible text.",
      "status": "ok"
    },
