      "justification": "The paper's description of Figure 3 lists many nodes generically as 'concepts' and 'connections' without explaining the specific semantics distinguishing origination/development/scaffolding node types in the figure itself, supporting the critique.",
      "status": "ok"
    },
    {
      "method": "baseline_cmp3_baseline_v2",
      "paper_id": "1E4Bltg6Xb",
      "weakness": "Limited novelty relative to existing work: policy attention is essentially precomputed shortest-path subgraph selection and n-hop neighborhoods is a standard graph operation, not adequately differentiated from prior graph sparsification/attention-based methods.",
      "reliable": 1,
      "error_type": "",
      "justification": "The paper's related work section does not compare or contrast DFR's components against existing graph sparsification/subgraph extraction techniques beyond citing them briefly, so the novelty claim is not substantiated.",
